# =====================================================================
# SGS Frontend — Environment variables template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust the values for your environment:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# All variables are exposed to the client bundle (Vite only forwards
# variables prefixed with `VITE_`). Never put secrets in here —
# everything under VITE_ is readable in the browser.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# API (architecture.md §7 — Central Axios client)
# Base URL of the Spring Boot REST API. All feature API modules
# (src/features/*/api) resolve paths against this URL via src/api/client.ts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development: SAME-ORIGIN via the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.ts proxies
# /api → http://localhost:8081). This avoids CORS entirely — the backend omits
# CORS headers on its security rejections (403 empty-body), which become
# opaque browser errors when calling it cross-origin. Only override this with
# an absolute URL (e.g. http://localhost:8081/api) when the proxy is NOT in
# front of the API and the backend's CORS config is known to be complete.
VITE_API_URL=/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# App metadata (build identity, shown by error reporting / headers)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_APP_NAME=SGS

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature flags (optional — prefix custom flags with VITE_ENABLE_)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_ENABLE_NOTIFICATIONS_POLLING=true
